answer:
Use Vue’s `onMounted()` lifecycle hook. Register it synchronously during component setup; its callback runs after the component’s initial render, when its DOM tree has been created and inserted into the parent container.

```vue
<script setup>
import { onMounted } from 'vue'

onMounted(() => {
  // Access the component's DOM here
})
</script>
```

Use the Composition API’s `onMounted()` hook. Register its callback synchronously during `setup()`; it runs after the component’s DOM tree has been created and inserted into its parent container.

```vue
<script setup>
import { onMounted } from 'vue'

onMounted(() => {
  // Access or work with the component's rendered DOM here
})
</script>
```

Use the `onMounted` lifecycle hook. It runs after the component’s initial render, when its DOM nodes have been created:

```vue
<script setup>
import { onMounted } from 'vue'

onMounted(() => {
  // Run code after the component's DOM exists
})
</script>
```

Register the hook synchronously during component setup.
